  "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $p$ that satisfy both $p-2>3$ and $1-2p\\le -7$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $p-2>3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p-2 & >3 \\\\ p-2+2 & >3+2 \\\\ p & >5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252107/assets/1189f49b694afcfef7f10a19b523ebbcce3bb8ab13b69e60ebfd5a6c342ff10e.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $1-2p\\le -7\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2p & \\le -7 \\\\ 1-2p-1 & \\le -7-1 \\\\ -2p & \\le -8 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2p) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ 2p & \\ge 8 \\\\ \\frac{2p}{2} & \\ge \\frac{8}{2} \\\\ p & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252107/assets/f8bf3ae94c8048dcf9060c985300f9a808ae73158eeeef6e0f01f3f922d33ea9.png)\n\nTo find the values of $p$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252107/assets/1a4cd0c86983a39354eef09ad60d44f3815c082f443a3eb12bd14f6232988f65.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $p\\in (5,\\infty ).$",
